AWS EC2 KEY PAIR 

In Amazon Ec2 , a key pair  is used to securely connect to your server(instances)  

It replaces password
It consits of: 
* Public  Key -> stored in AWS (on your Ec2 instance)
* Private  key -> downloaded by you (.pem file)

How it works:
  When you try to connect 
  1. YOu use your private key(.pem file)
  2. AWS checks it with the public key on the server
  3. If it matches - access granted 

We use this because?
  AWS disables password login by default because:
   * password can be hacked or cracked using the brute force method 
   * Key pair are much more secure 
